#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:217
msgid ""
"To upload EEPROM data (from EEMEM directive) you need to use ``uploadeep`` "
"target instead ``upload`` for :option:`pio run --target` command. For "
"example, ``pio run -t uploadeep``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:222
msgid "Erase chip before programming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:224
msgid ""
"In some cases erasing chip memory is a mandatory procedure before uploading "
"bootloader or setting fuses. AVRDUDE provides a special flag ``-e`` that "
"causes a chip erase to be executed. This will reset the contents of the "
"flash ROM and EEPROM to the value ``0xff``, and clear all lock bits. The "
"easiest way to use it is to add this flag via the :ref:"
"`projectconf_upload_flags` option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:240
msgid "Fuses programming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:242
msgid ""
"PlatformIO has a built-in target called ``fuses`` for setting fuse bits. The "
"default fuse bits are predefined in the board manifest file in the ``fuses`` "
"section. For example, `fuses section for Arduino Uno board <https://github."
"com/platformio/platform-atmelavr/blob/develop/boards/uno.json>`_. To set "
"fuse bits you need to use target ``fuses`` with :option:`pio run --target` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:248
msgid "Custom fuses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:250
msgid ""
"Custom fuse values and upload flags (based on upload protocol) should be "
"specified in :ref:`projectconf`. The ``lfuse`` and ``hfuse`` bits are "
"mandatory, ``efuse`` is optional and not supported by all targets. An "
"example of setting custom fuses for ``uno`` board:"
msgstr ""

