#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:463
msgid "Bootloader programming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:465
msgid ""
"PlatformIO has a built-in target called ``bootloader`` for flashing "
"bootloaders. The default bootloader image and corresponding fuse bits are "
"predefined in the board manifest file in the ``bootloader`` section, for "
"example, `Arduino Uno <https://github.com/platformio/platform-atmelavr/blob/"
"develop/boards/uno.json>`_. To upload a bootloader image you need to use "
"target ``bootloader`` with :option:`pio run --target` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:472
msgid "Custom bootloader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:474
msgid ""
"Custom bootloader and accompanying fuses should be specified in :ref:"
"`projectconf`. If ``lock_bits`` and ``unlock_bits`` are not set then the "
"default values ``0x0F`` and ``0x3F`` are used accordingly. An example of "
"setting custom bootloader for ``uno`` board:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/atmelavr_extra.rst:493
msgid ""
"``MiniCore``, ``MegaCore``, ``MightyCore`` and ``MajorCore`` have a wide "
"variety of precompiled bootloaders. Bootloader binaries are dynamically "
"selected according to the hardware parameters ``f_cpu``, ``oscillator``, "
"``uart`` and ``upload_speed``. For a complete table with all available baud "
"rates, see the `Optiboot flash repo <https://github.com/MCUdude/"
"optiboot_flash>`_. Here is a table with recommended baud rates for different "
"clock frequencies:"
msgstr ""

